  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1604.01 Maximum Sulfur Content Allowable in Coal",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1604.01 Maximum Sulfur Content Allowable in Coal.\n\n(a) For a coal-burning device placed in operation before April 15, 1970 the sulfur content of coal burned in the device shall not exceed 2.8 pounds per million BTU gross heat content.\n\n(b) For a coal-burning device placed in operation on or after April 15, 1970:\n\n(1) The sulfur content of coal burned in the device shall not exceed 1.5 pounds per million BTU gross heat content; and\n\n(2) The sulfur content of coal burned in the device shall not exceed 1.0 pound per million BTU gross heat content, averaged over any consecutive 3-month period.\n\nSource. #6519-B, eff 5-29-97 (from Env-A 402.02); ss by #8330, eff 4-23-05; ss by #10415, eff 9-24-13 (from Env-A 1606.01); ss by #12694, eff 12-22-18; ss by #13808, eff 11-18-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1600.html"
